facts:
$k>0$ opens the parabola upward (**concave up**), and $k<0$ opens it downward (**concave down**).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-3.6, xmax=3.6, ymin=-5, ymax=5, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=-2.15:2.15] {x*x};
\addplot[smooth, thick, red, dashed, <->, domain=-2.15:2.15] {-x*x};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:3.0,3.2) {$k>0$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:3.0,-3.2) {$k<0$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$|k|>1$ makes the parabola **narrower** than $y=x^2$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.6, xmax=4.6, ymin=-1.2, ymax=5.6, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth, thick, dashed, <->, domain=-1.87:1.87] {x*x};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=-1.29:1.29] {3*x*x};
\node[anchor=east] at (axis cs:-2.3,3.5) {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[anchor=west, blue] at (axis cs:1.6,5.0) {$|k|>1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$0<|k|<1$ makes it **wider** than $y=x^2$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-5.4, xmax=5.4, ymin=-1.2, ymax=4.6, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth, thick, dashed, <->, domain=-1.87:1.87] {x*x};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=-3:3] {0.3*x*x};
\node[anchor=east] at (axis cs:-2.2,3.5) {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[anchor=west, blue] at (axis cs:3.3,2.7) {$0<|k|<1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$b$ translates the graph horizontally with the sign flipped: $y=(x-3)^2$ moves **right** $3$ and $y=(x+3)^2$ moves **left** $3$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.4, xmax=6.8, ymin=-2.0, ymax=4.8, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth, thick, dashed, <->, domain=-1.87:1.87] {x*x};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=1.13:4.87] {(x-3)*(x-3)};
\addplot[-{Stealth}, thick] coordinates {(0,-0.9) (3,-0.9)};
\node[below] at (axis cs:1.5,-0.95) {$b$};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*, blue] coordinates {(3,0)};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:-4.3,3.5) {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[anchor=east, blue] at (axis cs:6.7,4.3) {$y=(x-b)^{2}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$c$ translates the graph vertically: **up** $c$ when $c>0$ and **down** $|c|$ when $c<0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-5.0, xmax=5.0, ymin=-1.2, ymax=6.8, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth, thick, dashed, <->, domain=-2.2:2.2] {x*x};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=-2.14:2.14] {x*x+2};
\addplot[-{Stealth}, thick] coordinates {(-3.4,0) (-3.4,2)};
\node[anchor=east] at (axis cs:-3.5,1.0) {$c$};
\node[anchor=east] at (axis cs:-2.9,4.6) {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[anchor=west, blue] at (axis cs:2.5,6.3) {$y=x^{2}+c$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

